node_modules/
# Build output only — anchored so it never swallows a source dir named lib/
# (e.g. src/lib). An unanchored rule here silently excluded wire.ts and cache.ts once
# already; the package then built locally from untracked files and failed in CI.
/lib/
/lib-test/
*.js.map
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
coverage/
package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
CLAUDE.md

# Superpowers execution scaffolding. Plans and SDD ledgers quote live-org detail
# (product names, counts, failed reads) as a matter of course, and this repository is
# public. The other two repos are ignored only by a `*` gitignore the tool happens to
# write inside the directory; a rule here does not depend on that file existing.
/.superpowers/
